---
// Shells 分类聚合页（CollectionPage）—— 方案 5.1
// 表格形式：名称 | 描述 | 已知能力 | 获取方式 | 确认状态。
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MediaFigure from '../../components/MediaFigure.astro';
import { SITE_IMAGES } from '../../data/images';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import PreReleaseNotice from '../../components/PreReleaseNotice.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import { SHELLS, PREQUEL_ONLY_SHELLS, SHELL_CLASSIFICATION_NOTE, SHELL_BONDING } from '../../data/shells';

const title = 'Mortal Shell 2 Shells — All 8 Shell Names & Unlock Rates';
const description =
  'All eight Mortal Shell 2 Shells — Tiel, Proxima, Eredrim, Smert, Gragu, Sariel, Sester Genessa, Lazlo — with unlock rates and the Tier IV bonding cap.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Shells', url: '/shells/' },
];

const officialCount = SHELLS.filter((s) => s.source.status === 'official').length;
const orderedByRate = [...SHELLS].filter((s) => typeof s.unlockRate === 'number');
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  schemaType="collection"
  breadcrumb={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />

  <PreReleaseNotice />
  <div class="mb-8">
    <MediaFigure
      src={SITE_IMAGES.shellsPortrait.src}
      alt={SITE_IMAGES.shellsPortrait.alt}
      width={SITE_IMAGES.shellsPortrait.width}
      height={SITE_IMAGES.shellsPortrait.height}
      credit={SITE_IMAGES.shellsPortrait.credit}
    />
  </div>

  <header class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ash-100 md:text-4xl">
      Mortal Shell 2 Shells Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-ash-400">
      Shells are the bodies you possess in combat, and Mortal Shell II has
      <strong>eight of them</strong>. All eight are now named:
      <a href="/tiel/" class="text-amber-glow hover:underline">Tiel</a>,
      <a href="/proxima/" class="text-amber-glow hover:underline">Proxima</a>,
      <a href="/eredrim/" class="text-amber-glow hover:underline">Eredrim</a>, Smert, Gragu, Sariel,
      Sester Genessa and Lazlo. Seven of their bodies sit near <strong>Zhirelle, the Shellkeeper</strong>
      and can be tracked by spending Gloom; Sester Genessa is the hidden one and has to be earned
      through a side quest. The table is <strong>sorted by global unlock rate</strong>, which is the
      closest published proxy for the order players find them.
      {officialCount} of {SHELLS.length} rows carry Official status; the rest rest on player-compiled
      routes and are labelled Community. No stats or abilities are published for any Shell, and this
      page does not invent them.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto surface-card">
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-ash-700 bg-ash-900/50 text-left text-ash-400">
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Shell</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Unlock achievement</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Global unlock</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Confirmed as a Shell by</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Known abilities</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Acquisition</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Status</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          SHELLS.map((shell) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5 align-top last:border-0 hover:bg-ash-900/35">
              <td class="px-4 py-3">
                <div class="font-semibold text-ash-100">
                  {shell.hasDetailPage ? (
                    <a href={shell.detailHref ?? `/shells/${shell.slug}/`} class="text-amber-glow hover:underline">
                      {shell.name}
                    </a>
                  ) : (
                    shell.name
                  )}
                </div>
                <div class="mt-1 text-ash-400">{shell.summary}</div>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-ash-300">{shell.unlockAchievement ?? '—'}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 tabular-nums text-ash-300">
                {typeof shell.unlockRate === 'number' ? `${shell.unlockRate}%` : '—'}
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-ash-400">{shell.shellConfirmedBy}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-ash-300">
                <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
                  {shell.knownAbilities.map((a) => (
                    <li>{a}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-ash-400">{shell.acquisition}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">
                <StatusBadge status={shell.source.status} size="sm" />
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <section class="prose-body mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-ash-300">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">How the eight names were identified</h2>
    <p>{SHELL_CLASSIFICATION_NOTE}</p>
    <p>
      The practical upshot: <strong>Sariel is the one row to treat with caution.</strong> Every other
      Shell on this table is named as a Shell by Cold Symmetry or by the Official Gameplay Reveal.
      Sariel is not, anywhere. If the retail roster turns out to differ from the eight above, that is
      the row that changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      The full list, including all 53 achievements and the thirteen Weapons and Sidearms, is on the
      <a href="/mortal-shell-2-achievements/" class="text-amber-glow hover:underline">achievements page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">What the unlock rates suggest about order</h2>
    <p>
      Tiel ({orderedByRate[0]?.unlockRate}%) and Proxima ({orderedByRate[1]?.unlockRate}%) are
      within two points of each other, so both are opening-hours acquisitions — Proxima is not a
      late unlock despite being new to the series. The first real drop is to Eredrim at
      {orderedByRate[2]?.unlockRate}%, and Smert and Gragu sit less than a point apart, which
      usually means two pickups in the same stretch of the game rather than a strict sequence.
      Lazlo is the rarest at {orderedByRate[7]?.unlockRate}%, making it the best candidate for a
      late Shell — and notably the hidden Sester Genessa at {orderedByRate[6]?.unlockRate}% is
      found by <em>more</em> players than Lazlo, so being hidden did not make her the hardest to get.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ash-500">
      Unlock percentages are a snapshot read on 1 September 2026, twelve days after release. They
      rise as more accounts play, and the gaps between them narrow over time. Order inferred from
      rates is a probability statement about where players find things, not a published route.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">Bonding caps at {SHELL_BONDING.maxTier}</h2>
    <p>
      Reaching the maximum bonding tier for one Shell at the Shellkeeper is its own achievement
      ("Decked Out", 46.9%). Community testing puts that cap at <strong>{SHELL_BONDING.maxTier}</strong>,
      costing roughly <strong>{SHELL_BONDING.glimpsesPerShell} Glimpses per Shell</strong> —
      about {SHELL_BONDING.glimpsesTotal} in total if you want it on all eight, which is what the
      "Seeking the Past" achievement (3.8%, the rarest in the game after the completion one) requires.
      Breaking a Glimpse Stone after twenty enemy kills reportedly yields three Glimpses, and up to
      thirteen Glimpse Stones can be bought from the hub merchant. Those figures come from a
      player-compiled guide, not from the developer.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">Prequel Shells that did not return</h2>
    <p>
      {PREQUEL_ONLY_SHELLS.join(' and ')} were Shells in Mortal Shell (2020). Neither appears
      anywhere in the retail achievement list, and the eight names above already account for the
      full roster. Earlier drafts of this page listed Harros as the probable starting Shell on the
      strength of the first game; that guess is now retired.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ash-500">
      Detailed Shell pages (with stat tables, upgrade paths, and recommended builds) are expanded
      only when a real acquisition route and reproducible current-build details are recorded. Until
      then, each uncertainty stays visible instead of being guessed.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
